• - `scripts/land/train.sh:100,137-145` and `scripts/push-both.sh:54,59-67` — the stale-clone guard compares the remote against overridable `LAND_REPO`, not the canonical repository. A genuinely stale clone with both `origin=…/unbalancedparentheses/concrete2` and the old `LAND_REPO=unbalancedparentheses/concrete2` passes validation and pushes to the archived repository. **Fix:** validate GitHub push destinations against a non-overridable `lambdaclass/concrete` constant; keep `LAND_REPO` only as the `gh` test override. Add this old-origin/old-environment combination as a refusal test.

  - `scripts/land/train.sh:139`, `scripts/push-both.sh:59`, and `scripts/land/install-bot.sh:42-45` — only `remote.<name>.url` is checked. Git pushes instead to `remote.<name>.pushurl` when configured, so a clone can fetch from lambdaclass/concrete while still pushing to concrete2. The installer’s “repointing” also leaves that push URL untouched. **Fix:** validate every effective destination with `git remote get-url --push --all`; when migrating the bot clone, remove or replace stale `pushurl` entries. Add a differing-fetch/push-URL fixture.

  - `scripts/land/train.sh:435,521-566` — `check` never calls `require_remote_repo`, although its default remote leg pushes `wip/land-*`. An existing train whose origin has become stale can therefore publish to concrete2 before `ci` or `land` would refuse it. **Fix:** validate before starting any check legs, ideally also inside `remote_leg` as defense in depth, and cover `check` in `scripts/checks/landing_script.sh`.

  - `scripts/land/bot.sh:139-143,239,450-490` — the bot has no repository validation before fetching, auto-rebasing, pushing rebased branches, or publishing notes. In particular, `bot.sh rebase` reaches the push at line 239 without invoking any guarded train command. **Fix:** run the shared canonical-remote check at bot startup before `sync_remote`, and test stale-origin `tick` and `rebase` with assertions that no branch or note moved.

  - `scripts/land/install-bot.sh:92-96` — an existing installation’s old `LAND_REPO=unbalancedparentheses/concrete2` is retained with only a warning. After origin is repointed, the installed bot cannot build, dispatch, or land because its GitHub repository and remote disagree, yet installation reports success. **Fix:** migrate the existing `LAND_REPO` line to lambdaclass/concrete, or fail installation explicitly until it is corrected.

  - `docs/LANDING.md:416,491` and `ROADMAP.md:174,517` — current operational documentation still requires write access to “both repositories,” displays “both mains,” and says the move lands on “both remotes.” **Fix:** change these to the single lambdaclass/concrete main; leave only archival documents describing the former mirror topology.

